cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Si utiliza este software, por favor cítelo como se indica a
  continuación.
title: >-
  Same function, different pruning: the dominant direction of W_O
  under free, soft, and hard intervention
abstract: >-
  Code and measurement scripts for a study of the value-output gauge
  in Vision Transformer attention heads. The dominant direction of a
  head's output projection, v1(W_O), is routinely used to prune
  redundant heads, interpret their role, or route information between
  them; this work shows that direction is not identifiable under the
  value-output gauge, that the non-identifiability has a measurable
  consequence for pruning decisions, and that the coupling between
  that geometry and the function is one-directional across a soft
  angular probe and a hard simplex-imposing variant. Results are
  established on ViT-B/16, contrasted on ViT-L/16 and a frozen
  DINOv2, and extended without training to a pretrained language
  transformer (Pythia-410M).
type: software
